> Check a refinement-depth family

For a unary n-state chain ending in one accepting loop, every state has a
different distance to acceptance. Each proper refinement peels off the next
predecessor. For n at least2, n−2 proper growth passes are followed by one
stable pass, giving n−1 total rounds. The singleton needs one stable pass.
Actual state visits are n times the number of rounds, and transition reads are
the same because the alphabet has one symbol.

The finite sweep verifies these exact selected-work counts. Ordered vector-key
maps add lexicographic and tree-comparison work; the full implementation
therefore has a conservative O((k+1)*n squared*log(n+1)) bound, rather than
inferring total runtime from state visits alone. Ordinary driver/output storage
is O(n*(k+1)); optional captured round history can be quadratic in n or larger
with alphabet size.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/moore_scaling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/dfa_minimization.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, visits, formula;
    std::print("| chain states | actual quotient states | actual rounds | actual state visits | exact visit " "formula | actual transition reads | map comparisons |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int n : {1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}) {
        auto r =
            dm::algorithms::moore_minimize_run(dm::algorithms::moore_chain_dfa(
                                               n));
        auto expected = n * std::max(1, n - 1);
        x.push_back(n);
        visits.push_back(r.work.state_visits);
        formula.push_back(expected);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n,
                   r.result.num_states, r.work.rounds, r.work.state_visits,
                   expected, r.work.transition_reads, r.work.map_comparisons);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, formula, "chain visit formula", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(
        x, visits, "actual state visits", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Unary chains: actual Moore state visits").x_label("completed states n").y_label("state signature visits").save_svg("build/moore_scaling.svg");
}
```
